{
  "name": "Get a Slack alert when a Walmart or Target product is back in stock",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1de3b2a6-d7f8-4494-bb02-5d9836f0bd6b",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Get a Slack alert when a Walmart or Target product is back in stock\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Every hour, Scrapio checks the live availability and price for each product in your watchlist.\n2. Each check is logged to a history sheet, and the watchlist row is updated with the latest status.\n3. A product that just came back in stock, or dropped in price, posts an alert to Slack.\n4. A separate weekly branch reads the history and posts a restock and price-drop digest to Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Add your Scrapio API credential (get a key at app.scrapio.dev) and enable the free Commerce add-on for your plan\n- [ ] Create a Google Sheet named Watchlist with columns: retailer, product_id, title, last_in_stock, last_price\n- [ ] Add a row per product (retailer is walmart or target; last_in_stock can start as false)\n- [ ] Connect your Google Sheet in Read Watchlist, Append Check to History Sheet, Update Watchlist Row, and Read Stock History\n- [ ] Add your Slack credential and channel IDs to the two alert nodes and Send Weekly Stock Digest to Slack\n- [ ] Activate the workflow\n\n### Customization tips\n\nLower the schedule interval to catch restocks faster, or add another retailer by extending Route by Retailer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
